.TH CHM-RUN-COMPATIBLE-BINARY 1
.SH NAME
chm-run-compatible-binary \- inspect a binary and optionally select a reviewed execution runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chm-run-compatible-binary
.RI [ --json ]
.I FILE
.br
.B chm-run-compatible-binary
.RI [ --dry-run | --run ]
.RI [ --sysroot " DIR" ]
.RI [ --timeout " SECONDS" ]
.I FILE
.RI [ -- " ARG..." ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects executable headers before choosing an execution route. ELF files use the native Linux loader when the host architecture matches, otherwise a matching QEMU user-mode runner is required. Windows PE files use Wine on Linux or the native Windows loader. Mach-O runs natively on macOS; Linux may use the optional Darling compatibility layer when installed, or a full macOS environment. DOS MZ files use DOSBox or DOSBox-X. WebAssembly uses Wasmtime or Wasmer; JAR files use Java.
.PP
Inspection is the default and does not execute the file. The selected runtime is displayed explicitly. This tool does not download proprietary operating-system binaries, bypass code signing, or certify ABI compatibility.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print the header report as JSON.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show the selected runtime command without executing it.
.TP
.B --run
Execute using the selected runtime.
.TP
.B --sysroot DIR
Supply a Linux sysroot to QEMU user-mode.
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Set the maximum execution time (default 60 seconds).
.TP
.B --
Separate the binary path from arguments passed to the runtime.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on successful inspection or execution; nonzero for unknown formats, unavailable runtimes, invalid arguments, or execution failure.
